  "subject": "A 70-year-old hand-cranked level-crossing keeper on a Huwei sugar railway lowers the barrier at 3:15 for the one slow tourist train a day, and has waited eleven years beside the same woman on a scooter without asking her name, until the day the train is cancelled and neither of them leaves.",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien chamber folk ballad, unhurried and spare. Concert harp playing slow rolling arpeggios in open fifths; solo cello bowing long low legato lines with a warm woody tone; soft fingerpicked nylon guitar tracing a steady two-bar pattern. Intimate dry chamber-room mix, harp and cello in front, plain close vocal. Male baritone, plain and restrained, mid-low register, clearly sung melody, one lead voice. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 72 BPM, D major. Slow, patient, companionable mood. No rap, no drums, no autotune, no synth pads, no electric guitar, no EDM drop.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n三點一刻 我共柵欄放落\n手搖的鐵桿 慢慢仔斜\n糖廠的細火車 一工干焦一班\n行甲比行路 閣較慢\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n對面彼个阿姨 騎機車停佇線邊\n十一冬矣 伊攏準時到\n\n[Chorus]\n等 等彼班車 等彼班車\n柵欄落落去 咱兩人就無緊\n等 等彼班車 等彼班車\n你毋講名 我嘛毋問\n\n[Verse]\n伊的菜籃仔 掛佇車頭\n有時一把蔥 有時一包豆乾\n我共鈴仔搖 叮叮\n伊講 你搖甲比車較大聲\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n五節車廂 慢慢仔過\n伊閣講 今仔日比昨昏較慢\n\n[Chorus]\n等 等彼班車 等彼班車\n柵欄落落去 咱兩人就無緊\n等 等彼班車 等彼班車\n毋講名 嘛知影 你是誰\n\n[Verse]\n今仔日 公所講 車停駛\n我猶原三點一刻 去放柵欄\n對面 伊嘛猶原 騎車到\n兩个人 看空空的鐵枝路\n\n[Bridge]\n無車 嘛愛等\n等的人 比車較早到\n\n[Chorus]\n等 等彼班車 等彼班車\n柵欄落落去 咱兩人就無緊\n等 等無車 嘛是等\n你敢欲 坐佇我的椅仔邊\n\n[Outro]\n鐵桿慢慢仔 起來\n路 閣再開",
